[The Joint Mathematics Meetings 2025](https://jointmathematicsmeetings.org/meetings/national/jmm2025/2314_program.html) will take place in Seattle, WA, Jan 8-11.

I will speak in an AMS Special Session on "[Modeling and Optimization on Graph-Structured Data](https://jointmathematicsmeetings.org/meetings/national/jmm2025/2314_program_ss81.html#title)". The talk "Linear independent component analysis in Wasserstein space" is based on joint work with Caroline Moosmueller and Chuxiangbo Wang.

Special thanks to MRC 2024 for their generous travel support. I look forward to meeting my fellow MRC participants at the 2024 summer conference on [Mathematics of Adversarial, Interpretable, and Explainable AI](https://www.ams.org/programs/research-communities/2024MRC-AI) and other MRC alumni.

The MRC special sessions are scheduled for Thursday, January 9, 8:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m. and 1:00 p.m. – 5:00 p.m. 
